20	/****************************************************************************
21	 * Bit-bang SPI driver for the GC9D01 160x160 RGB565 LCD on BK7258 DevKit.
22	 *
23	 * Pin mapping (from schematic, confirmed against ARMINO gpio_map.h):
24	 *   SCLK = GPIO_2  (QSPI1_CLK, func6 — unused for bit-bang)
25	 *   CS   = GPIO_3  (QSPI1_CSN, func6 — unused for bit-bang)
26	 *   MOSI = GPIO_4  (QSPI1_IO0, func6 — unused for bit-bang)
27	 *   DC   = GPIO_5  (QSPI1_IO1, func6 — unused for bit-bang)
28	 *   RST  = GPIO_29 (LCD_RST on schematic, pin 65)
29	 *   BL   = GPIO_25 (LCD_BL_PWM via Q3)
30	 *
31	 * The GC9D01 uses a separate DC pin (not 9-bit SPI).  DC=LOW for command,
32	 * DC=HIGH for data.  SPI mode 0, MSB first.
33	 *
34	 * Staged test via NSH command "lcdtest":
35	 *   lcdtest          — staged bring-up (A=backlight, B=init, C=red sq)
36	 *   lcdtest go       — one-step reliable LCD bring-up (production flow)
37	 *   lcdtest pwr lo hi — power-on GPIO range for binary-search
38	 *   lcdtest scan     — GPIO pin scan for LCD power enable
39	 ****************************************************************************/
